# `a&&b` without spaces: the fix adds them.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where a&&b
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..31
  PIPELINE@0..30
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..30
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..30
        NAME_REF@26..27
          IDENT@26..27 "a"
        AMP2@27..29 "&&"
        NAME_REF@29..30
          IDENT@29..30 "b"
  WHITESPACE@30..31 "\n"

error[DS0111]: `&&` is not an operator
  --> query:1:28
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where a&&b
  |                            ^^ this is C's "and"
  |
  = help: use `and` to require both conditions: `a and b`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where a and b
which parses without errors
